-- title:
--   An open set containing infinitely many κ-points of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N$, and write $R=\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec} R$ be a proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ morphism with $X$ integral. The following data are assumed: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the modular function field $F_N=\mathbb{Q}(q\text{-expansions } j_{q,d},\, d\mid N)$ — that is, an integral, proper, smooth relative-dimension-one $\mathbb{Q}$-scheme together with an isomorphism of $F_N$ with its function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ and a bijection from its closed points to the places of $F_N/\mathbb{Q}$ matching stalks with valuation subrings — with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto the fibre $X\times_R\mathbb{Q}$ over the base; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0$ whose place is the cusp $\infty$, realised by a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of $X\times_R\mathbb{Q}$ lying on $\varepsilon_\infty$ and mapping to $x_0$ through $e_0^{-1}$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the base-changed function field, isomorphic over the base to $X\times_R\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, whose point–place dictionary is Galois equivariant (`hgal`) and compatible with that of $M_0$ by restriction of valuation subrings along the base-change isomorphism (`hcompat`); for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p\in A$ non-invertible, a lift $\rho_A\colon R\to A$ of the inclusion $R\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a curve model $M_s(A)$ over the residue field of $A$ of the corresponding modular function field, isomorphic over the base to $X\times_R\kappa_A$, and, when $\kappa_A$ is algebraically closed, a degree-preserving reduction map $r$ on places which matches orders of reductions of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ and is compatible with reduction of points (`hsp`). Finally let $s$ be a closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ such that the image of $x_0$ in $X$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, let $A$ be such a valuation subring with algebraically closed residue field, assume the ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\varepsilon_\infty(s)}$ generated by the germ of the image of $p$ is prime, and let $U$ be an open subset of $X$ containing the point of $X$ that this prime ideal determines through `X.fromSpecStalk`. Then the set of $\kappa_A$-points of $M_s(A)$ (sections of its structure morphism) whose image in $X$, under the isomorphism $e_s$ followed by the first projection, lies in $U$ is infinite.
--
--   This is the fibre-density step: an open subset of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-model of $X_0(N)$ meeting the generic point of the special fibre receives infinitely many $\kappa$-points of the geometric special fibre, the closed points of a smooth proper integral curve over an algebraically closed field being infinite in number while the complement of a non-empty open subset is finite. It feeds the two $q$-expansion arguments [`ModularCurve.false_of_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_pow_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.false_of_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_pow_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero) and [`ModularCurve.false_of_pow_mul_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.false_of_pow_mul_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero).
